Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: cargo-deny
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny/issues
Source: https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny
Comment:
 The vendor/ directory contains the crates.io dependencies of cargo-deny,
 produced by `cargo vendor`. The stanzas for vendor/ are generated from
 debian/copyright.in by debian/gen-copyright; see debian/README.source.
 Edit debian/copyright.in rather than this file.

Files: *
Copyright: 2019-2026 Embark Studios
License: Expat or Apache-2.0

Files: debian/*
Copyright: 2024-2026 Pexip AS
License: Expat or Apache-2.0

Files: examples/14_license_detection/LICENSE-*
Copyright: 2019-2026 Embark Studios
License: Expat or Apache-2.0
Comment: Licence texts (AGPL-3.0, FreeBSD, MIT variants) used as test
 fixtures for cargo-deny's licence detection; they are not the licence of
 any code in this package.

Files: tests/snapshots/advisories__*.snap
Copyright: 2019-2026 Embark Studios
           RustSec advisory database contributors
License: Expat or Apache-2.0, and CC0-1.0
Comment: Test snapshots that include advisory text from the RustSec advisory
 database, which is released under CC0-1.0.

